      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "1. Find the inverse function $f^{-1}(x)$ of $f(x)$ and simplify it.\n2. Calculate $f^{-1}(x)$.\n3. Calculate $f((2x)^{-1})$.\n4. Equate $f^{-1}(x)$ and $f((2x)^{-1})$ and solve for $x$.\n5. Sum the roots obtained from step 4.\nStep 1: Find the inverse function $f^{-1}(x)$ of $f(x)$.\n$$f^{-1}(x) = \\frac{x-3}{16}.$$\n\nStep 2: Calculate $f^{-1}(x)$.\n$$f^{-1}(x) = \\frac{x-3}{16}.$$\n\nStep 3: Calculate $f((2x)^{-1})$.\n$$f((2x)^{-1}) = f\\left(\\frac{1}{2x}\\right) = 16\\cdot\\frac{1}{2x} + 3 = \\frac{8}{x} + 3.$$\n\nStep 4: Equate $f^{-1}(x)$ and $f((2x)^{-1})$ and solve for $x$.\n$$\\frac{x-3}{16} = \\frac{8}{x} + 3.$$\n\nStep 5: Sum the roots obtained from step 4.\n$$\\frac{x-3}{16} = \\frac{8 + 3x}{16} \\quad \\text{take common denominator:}$$\n$$x - 3 = 8 + 3x \\quad \\text{simplify:}$$\n$$-2x = 11 \\quad \\text{solve for x:}$$\n$$x = -\\frac{11}{2}.$$\nThe sum of the roots is: $$-\\frac{11}{2}.$$\nThe final answer is \\boxed{-\\frac{11}{2}}.",
