      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "Since $f^{-1}(x)=16^{-1}\\cdot x^{-1}-\\frac{3}{16}$,\n$f(x)=16^{-1}\\cdot x^{-1}-\\frac{3}{16}=f((2x)^{-1})$ $\\Longleftrightarrow$ $16^{-1}\\cdot x^{-1}-\\frac{3}{16}=x$ $\\Longleftrightarrow$ $y=\\frac{3}{16}+\\frac{1}{x^{-1}}$ $\\Longleftrightarrow$ $xy-1=3$ $\\Longleftrightarrow$ $(x+1)(y-3)=0$.\nHence, $x=-1, y=3$ or $x=1, y=3$.\nThen, $-1+1\\boxed{1}$.\nTo solve the equation \\( f(x)=16x+3 \\) and find the sum of all \\( x \\) that satisfy \\( f^{-1}(x)=f((2x)^{-1}) \\), we start by finding the inverse function \\( f^{-1}(x) \\).\n\nThe original function is \\( f(x) = 16x + 3 \\). To find the inverse, we set \\( y = f(x) \\):\n\n\\[ y = 16x + 3 \\]\n\nSolving for \\( x \\):\n\n\\[ y - 3 = 16x \\]\n\\[ x = \\frac{y - 3}{16} \\]\n\nThus, the inverse function is:\n\n\\[ f^{-1}(x) = \\frac{x - 3}{16} \\]\n\nNext, we are given the equation:\n\n\\[ f^{-1}(x) = f\\left(\\frac{1}{2x}\\right) \\]\n\nAnd we know that \\( f(x) = 16x + 3 \\). So, we substitute \\( x \\) with \\( \\frac{1}{2x} \\) in the function \\( f \\):\n\n\\[ f\\left(\\frac{1}{2x}\\right) = 16 \\cdot \\frac{1}{2x} + 3 = \\frac{8}{x} + 3 \\]\n\nNow, we set the inverse function equal to this expression:\n\n\\[ \\frac{x - 3}{16} = \\frac{8}{x} + 3 \\]\n\nWe need to solve this equation for \\( x \\):\n\n\\[ \\frac{x - 3}{16} = \\frac{8x + 48}{x} \\]\n\nClearing the denominators, we multiply both sides by \\( 16x \\):\n\n\\[ x(x - 3) = 16(8x + 48) \\]\n\\[ x^2 - 3x = 128x + 768 \\]\n\\[ x^2 - 131x - 768 = 0 \\]\n\nThis is a quadratic equation, and we solve it using the quadratic formula \\( x = \\frac{-b \\pm \\sqrt{b^2 - 4ac}}{2a} \\):\n\nHere, \\( a = 1 \\), \\( b = -131 \\), and \\( c = -768 \\):\n\n\\[ x = \\frac{-(-131) \\pm \\sqrt{(-131)^2 - 4 \\cdot 1 \\cdot (-768)}}{2 \\cdot 1} \\]\n\\[ x = \\frac{131 \\pm \\sqrt{17161 + 3072}}{2} \\]\n\\[ x = \\frac{131 \\pm \\sqrt{20233}}{2} \\]\n\nThus, the solutions are:\n\n\\[ x_1 = \\frac{131 + \\sqrt{20233}}{2} \\]\n\\[ x_2 = \\frac{131 - \\sqrt{20233}}{2} \\]\n\nWe need to find the sum of these solutions. By Vieta's formulas, the sum of the roots of the quadratic equation \\( ax^2 + bx + c = 0 \\) is given by \\( -\\frac{b}{a} \\).\n\nFor our equation \\( x^2 - 131x - 768 = 0 \\):\n\n\\[ a = 1 \\]\n\\[ b = -131 \\]\n\nSo, the sum of the roots is:\n\n\\[ -\\frac{-131}{1} = 131 \\]\n\nTherefore, the sum of all \\( x \\) that satisfy the given equation is:\n\n\\[ \\boxed{131} \\]",
